WEBVTT

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:08.290
Not many men are so privileged as we are

00:00:08.290 --> 00:00:11.720
to see a new civilization born before our own eyes.

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:13.720
There are times in the streets of Virginia City

00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:16.600
when I question the use of the word civilization.

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:19.480
It is always that way with the new Hop Singh.

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:21.520
A diamond before it is polished

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:23.490
seems no more than a clot of dirt.

00:00:31.080 --> 00:00:39.180
Is this the American way to toast on an American occasion to your son on his 18th birthday?

00:00:39.180 --> 00:00:41.930
To my son Jimmy's American birthday.

00:00:41.930 --> 00:00:51.510
To the joining of the past and the present to create a finer future.

00:00:51.510 --> 00:00:58.600
You have honored my house, and now there is much to do.

00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:00.000
You are fortunate to know the cut.

00:01:00.030 --> 00:01:02.240
the Cartwright family so well, Hopsing.

00:01:02.240 --> 00:01:04.540
It pleases me to know that here in America,

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:07.160
the affection and respect of the sons for the father

00:01:07.160 --> 00:01:10.110
is as strong as it is in the land of our ancestors.

00:01:10.110 --> 00:01:12.580
- The Cartwrights have great respect for you, my uncle,

00:01:12.580 --> 00:01:14.890
and admiration for your son.

00:01:14.890 --> 00:01:17.690
- I am happy that the younger sons will honor us

00:01:17.690 --> 00:01:20.250
with their presence at the birthday party.

00:01:20.250 --> 00:01:23.880
And do not worry, Hopsing, your friend Hoss will be fed

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.180
as well as if you yourself did the cooking.

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:49.810
to me?

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:08.870
Yeah, you and me work good together, Billy Boy.

00:02:08.870 --> 00:02:11.950
Gonna have to clean a lot more of this dirt out of here

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:14.310
before Virginia City is a fit place to live.

00:02:34.120 --> 00:02:39.210
Little Jimmy, is it sure you love Trevor's nest for dinner at the Jimmy Chang's birthday party?

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.170
That's what Adam told us.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:44.270
For sure, I would like that.

00:02:45.150 --> 00:02:47.130
It's something to eat. You'll like it all night.

00:03:00.380 --> 00:03:09.160
What happened to your boy? What happened to your boy?

00:03:09.800 --> 00:03:10.640
Can you talk, Hopsing?

00:03:10.980 --> 00:03:13.100
Looks like he's been in a pretty bad fight.

00:03:13.500 --> 00:03:15.360
Yeah. Paul, Paul, let me help him in the house.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:18.460
You forget about Hopsing all right.

00:03:18.750 --> 00:03:20.150
His Chinese business owner.

00:03:24.600 --> 00:03:25.860
What do you mean by that, Paul?

00:03:28.130 --> 00:03:30.000
I think he's tangled up in one of them tongue things.

00:03:30.060 --> 00:03:34.950
heard about do you? No, I don't, son. The Tong is a protective organization composed of civilized

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:39.510
people. I wonder how much more this has been going on. A lot of it. Particularly in the

00:03:39.510 --> 00:03:44.990
California gold mines. I didn't think anybody had spread over the mountains. Why would anybody

00:03:44.990 --> 00:03:53.200
want to do a thing like this? Because Hopsing is Chinese. That's a crazy thing I've heard

00:03:53.200 --> 00:04:00.000
of, Paul. I feel like going in there and tearing that town apart board by board. No, you won't

00:04:00.060 --> 00:04:02.950
And you'll go to Jimmy Chang's birthday party tomorrow just as you planned.

00:04:02.950 --> 00:04:05.950
I suppose we just forget about the fact that somebody beat up on Hop Singh.

00:04:05.950 --> 00:04:09.950
We're not gonna forget about it, but we're not gonna stir up more trouble for the Chinese than they already have.

00:04:38.380 --> 00:04:39.640
Ah, you sure you got enough money?

00:04:39.640 --> 00:04:41.030
Oh, yes sir, Paul. We do.

00:04:41.030 --> 00:04:51.800
Jimmy Chang's present. We'll see you later, Jimmy Chang.

00:04:51.800 --> 00:04:55.160
Nice.

00:04:55.160 --> 00:04:58.690
I would like to buy...

00:04:58.690 --> 00:04:59.730
...small...

00:05:00.000 --> 00:05:01.620
American flag?

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:09.310
I, uh, plumb out of them flags, ain't ya, Hank?

00:05:09.310 --> 00:05:12.120
Yeah, that's right, I-I forgot.

00:05:12.120 --> 00:05:14.120
I don't have any American flags, Chang.

00:05:14.120 --> 00:05:14.950
I'm sorry.

00:05:14.950 --> 00:05:20.230
What are you sorry for?

00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:21.510
I don't have any.

00:05:21.510 --> 00:05:23.220
You'll have to go some other place.

00:05:23.220 --> 00:05:24.430
Uh, thank you.

00:05:24.430 --> 00:05:27.140
I will try Campbell's on C Street.

00:05:27.140 --> 00:05:29.990
You don't have none, either.

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:50.110
- Neither does anybody else in town.

00:05:50.110 --> 00:05:54.400
- Right, right, Mr. Vernon, Mr. Adam.

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:57.260
It would seem my early nephew feeds the food

00:05:57.260 --> 00:06:00.000
to bring good health, it would seem obscene

00:06:00.000 --> 00:06:01.970
My brother has a few extra servings, too.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:04.580
There's a big day in your life, Jane.

00:06:04.580 --> 00:06:06.790
We might have proud of that boy.

00:06:06.790 --> 00:06:10.160
Mr. Cartwright, could I ask you a question, please?

00:06:10.160 --> 00:06:11.970
Of course. Anything you want, you know that.

00:06:11.970 --> 00:06:15.930
There are customs of your people I do not understand.

00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:19.270
I'd wish for my son an American birthday party.

00:06:19.270 --> 00:06:22.670
I wouldn't worry about it. Just give him a cake with candles.

00:06:22.670 --> 00:06:26.720
Oh, yes. It must be candles, and not flags.

00:06:26.720 --> 00:06:28.330
What do you mean, Jane?

00:06:28.330 --> 00:06:30.000
I had thought to put Americans...

00:06:30.000 --> 00:06:33.690
flags on the cake, but I understand it is not permitted.

00:06:34.250 --> 00:06:34.970
Who says so?

00:06:36.330 --> 00:06:38.300
Oh, it's no matter.

00:06:40.600 --> 00:06:44.580
Chang, did Hammond refuse to sell you American flags to put on Jimmy's cake?

00:06:45.390 --> 00:06:46.290
I did not understand.

00:06:47.130 --> 00:06:48.370
I do not wish trouble.

00:07:05.240 --> 00:07:07.020
Adam, that sounds good to see you.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:09.640
What can I do for my favorite customers?

00:07:09.640 --> 00:07:13.250
We'd like to buy some American flags.

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:17.730
I don't have any of them little ones, man.

00:07:17.730 --> 00:07:20.760
And how did you know we wanted some of those little ones?

00:07:20.760 --> 00:07:22.980
You know, maybe we wanted a great big one.

00:07:22.980 --> 00:07:24.760
Well, do ya?

00:07:24.760 --> 00:07:26.280
You running the store now, Jesse?

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:30.000
I just take care of the fares, that's all.

00:07:31.240 --> 00:07:32.440
I'll then stick out of ours.

00:07:34.290 --> 00:07:36.490
You pack a grudge a long time, Adam.

00:07:37.850 --> 00:07:39.830
Well, how 'bout it, Hammett?

00:07:40.210 --> 00:07:41.810
I'm just sure we don't have none.

00:07:42.870 --> 00:07:45.950
Why don't you take a nice, hard look?

00:07:56.640 --> 00:07:57.330
I didn't know I...

00:08:01.630 --> 00:08:03.110
How much did you need?

00:08:04.260 --> 00:08:04.780
Eighteen.

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:07.860
They're to be put on a birthday cake.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:12.270
There's a few extra.

00:08:13.340 --> 00:08:13.960
That'll be a dollar.

00:08:19.410 --> 00:08:19.710
Thank you.

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:36.790
Let Jesse Tibbs get under his skin, that's right.

00:08:36.790 --> 00:08:39.090
Leave him a hired gun, and yet he walks around loose.

00:08:39.090 --> 00:08:43.760
He'll crap himself in time.

00:08:43.760 --> 00:08:58.160
Somebody to run for mayor, isn't it?

00:08:58.160 --> 00:08:58.640
Adam.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:04.520
Is Jesse Tibbs still a foreman of that ranch that Andy Fuhrman bought outside of Carson?

00:09:04.520 --> 00:09:12.680
As far as I know, I'm seeing a business with the flags with Lee Chang.

00:09:12.680 --> 00:09:16.080
Yeah, that sounds just about like the kind of tactics that Fuhrman would use.

00:09:16.080 --> 00:09:19.820
First they are additional, now the Chinese.

00:09:19.820 --> 00:09:22.310
America for the Americans.

00:09:22.310 --> 00:09:25.060
That's a pretty tired platform.

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:30.000
Adam, do me a favor, will you take these flags over to Lee Chang and tell him that Hammond just misunderstood him.

00:09:30.350 --> 00:09:31.070
What are you up to?

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:33.470
Somebody I want to talk to.

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:47.560
Ah, and Cartwright, I'm rightly honored.

00:09:48.440 --> 00:09:50.620
What if I owe the pleasure of this visit, Mr. Cartwright?

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:53.360
You don't have to go through any of the formalities, Mr. Follett.

00:09:53.590 --> 00:09:54.640
We've known each other sometime.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:58.820
Let's go together.

00:10:01.630 --> 00:10:15.040
to Ben? Only I don't call myself a lawyer. Folks get in trouble, eh? Come to me for nothing in the law says I can't charge a fee for help. Now, just what did you have on your mind?

00:10:15.040 --> 00:10:30.000
That's right. Andy, what's your platform? Virginia.

00:10:30.000 --> 00:10:35.860
Virginia City for Virginia City. Short, sweet, and to the point. You like that?

00:10:35.860 --> 00:10:37.520
Well, it depends on what it means.

00:10:37.520 --> 00:10:43.410
It means Virginia City belongs to the folks that made it what it is. It means we don't want outsiders.

00:10:43.410 --> 00:10:47.900
Well now, what's your definition of an outsider, Andy?

00:10:47.900 --> 00:10:52.910
Ben, you live outside the city and you can't vote for me anyhow, even if you would.

00:10:52.910 --> 00:10:55.990
But I'll be glad to spell it out for you, Andy.

00:10:55.990 --> 00:11:00.000
It means our town's being overrun by foreigners who are willing to work for nothing,

00:11:00.000 --> 00:11:03.540
And they're taking the bread and butter out of the bounds of folks like us who built this country.

00:11:05.480 --> 00:11:13.150
Now by foreigners, Andy, you mean the Irish, the Welsh, or the Chinese?

00:11:14.080 --> 00:11:17.070
Before you start giving me any of that high-flown talk about prejudice,

00:11:17.480 --> 00:11:21.700
you just stop and remember this camp's full of those same Irishmen and Welshmen and Cornishmen,

00:11:21.920 --> 00:11:23.570
and those are the people I mean to protect.

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:26.920
I wasn't going to give you any high-flown talk about prejudice, Andy.

00:11:26.920 --> 00:11:30.000
I just wanted to know where you stood.

00:11:32.590 --> 00:11:34.200
Does that mean you're against me, Ben?

00:11:34.200 --> 00:11:43.670
It means that if I find out that you or any of your boys had anything to do with beating up my cook,

00:11:43.670 --> 00:11:49.650
I'll tie a rope around you, and I'll drag you up and down Main Street.

00:11:49.650 --> 00:11:58.440
Ben, like I said before, you don't live in this city, and you can't vote for me no-huh.

00:11:58.440 --> 00:12:00.000
So why don't you just stay up?

00:12:00.030 --> 00:12:02.430
I guess you just invited me in.

00:12:02.430 --> 00:12:28.480
Just when I got a surprise birthday for the run-out dude, we would have to run into it.

00:12:31.630 --> 00:12:32.090
coming to.

00:13:11.070 --> 00:13:11.590
Hey, good looking.

00:13:30.000 --> 00:13:34.900
The Pierce kid? Or maybe him?

00:13:34.900 --> 00:13:37.130
What if I was?

00:13:37.130 --> 00:13:43.600
If I didn't know you was making fun, I'd slap your mouth.

00:13:43.600 --> 00:13:48.600
Suppose I'd tell your daddy what you just said.

00:13:48.600 --> 00:13:51.570
What do you think old JR did to you, huh?

00:13:51.570 --> 00:13:58.370
Now you just be nice and I won't tell.

00:13:58.370 --> 00:13:59.280
Of course.

00:14:00.030 --> 00:14:08.470
let go why don't you try and make me well you just made the biggest mistake of your life

00:14:08.470 --> 00:14:25.510
biggest mistake you'll ever make look at that that's all right my sorry

00:14:33.200 --> 00:14:34.710
Yes, and what?

00:14:34.710 --> 00:14:39.160
I didn't mean it, the way it sounded.

00:14:39.160 --> 00:14:43.150
It's alright, I'm used to it.

00:14:43.150 --> 00:14:48.820
Here, I'll put some water on it.

00:14:48.820 --> 00:14:51.650
Get into the house.

00:14:51.650 --> 00:14:52.340
But, father-

00:14:52.340 --> 00:14:54.660
Did you hear me?

00:14:54.660 --> 00:14:56.420
You disgraced my neck.

00:14:56.420 --> 00:14:58.270
Flocking yourself in front of this heathen.

00:14:58.270 --> 00:14:59.510
I was just helping you.

00:15:00.920 --> 00:15:02.940
And I thank Billy Wheeler for that.

00:15:02.940 --> 00:15:04.380
Fuck, say that.

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:08.370
Just before I threat you.

00:15:08.370 --> 00:15:09.890
I'm afraid of you, father.

00:15:09.890 --> 00:15:13.440
You haven't done anything any time I look at a boy you see evil.

00:15:13.440 --> 00:15:18.890
You've done it, Mr Ridley.

00:15:18.890 --> 00:15:19.470
Why?

00:15:33.840 --> 00:15:34.400
- Good.

00:16:01.950 --> 00:16:04.130
Told you it was the biggest mistake you ever made.

00:16:04.130 --> 00:16:07.200
I sure told you.

00:16:07.200 --> 00:16:21.170
I wouldn't be too worried if I was you, Lee Chang, by Jimmy. He'll be around in it.

00:16:21.170 --> 00:16:24.010
That old man Ridley probably gave him a few extra chores to do.

00:16:24.010 --> 00:16:25.770
You know, Mr. Ridley, he's tougher than nails.

00:16:25.770 --> 00:16:29.070
Oh, Jimmy not mine. He work hard. He'll do what Mr. Ridley tells him.

00:16:32.910 --> 00:16:33.840
What do you think, Austin?

00:16:33.840 --> 00:16:40.570
That boy's so dang anxious to make his college money. He's done forgot his own birthday party.

00:16:40.570 --> 00:16:42.640
Yeah, he's almost an hour late.

00:16:42.640 --> 00:16:52.440
What is it, my son?

00:16:52.440 --> 00:16:54.390
Chase him!

00:17:04.410 --> 00:17:10.260
Sally Ridley is dead. Her father shot her. It was an accident. They think I killed her.

00:17:11.020 --> 00:17:14.140
Now look, Jimmy, I want you to tell me the whole story right from the very beginning.

00:17:14.580 --> 00:17:19.300
It was an accident, Joe. I liked Sally. I wouldn't ever hurt her.

00:17:26.660 --> 00:17:29.710
Send them out, don't forget her!

00:17:33.200 --> 00:17:36.820
Just keep calm. Ain't nobody gonna hurt that boy.

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:49.430
We'll handle this thing proper. Little Joe, you gotta cover me.

00:17:49.430 --> 00:17:53.340
Lookin' for any fight we want is off.

00:17:53.340 --> 00:17:54.770
You ain't gettin' him.

00:17:54.770 --> 00:17:57.670
...somebody, and he's gonna get what's comin' to him.

00:17:57.670 --> 00:18:00.000
Now, that's a bit tasty, Billy. Suppose we...

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:06.000
We give them a choice. Either we take the boy, or we get a dog. What about it?

00:18:06.000 --> 00:18:09.830
Wait here.

00:18:09.830 --> 00:18:21.030
Will they take my son?

00:18:21.030 --> 00:18:25.310
No, Lee Chang. If anybody doesn't get taken around here, it's gonna be a little guilty.

00:18:25.310 --> 00:18:27.400
But you believe, Jimmy.

00:18:27.400 --> 00:18:29.480
Look, don't worry, Lee Chang.

00:18:30.000 --> 00:18:33.020
Jared Foster's a fair and honest man. He'll know the truth when he hears it.

00:18:33.020 --> 00:18:41.450
Father, in America, a man is innocent until proven guilty. Isn't that right, Hobbs?

00:18:41.450 --> 00:18:43.500
That's right, Jim.

00:18:43.500 --> 00:18:48.460
Let's go, Hobbs.

00:18:48.460 --> 00:18:52.080
Hobbs, Adam's gonna stop by for us. Tell him we're not at the jail.

00:19:06.910 --> 00:19:08.990
Why'd you let him hack? We could've strung him up.

00:19:08.990 --> 00:19:13.600
Hey, Billy, Billy. Don't you remember what Fulma said?

00:19:13.600 --> 00:19:22.480
What we do is let it boil. We just let it boil.

00:19:22.480 --> 00:19:29.700
Now you've told me the whole truth. You sure you've left nothing.

00:19:34.570 --> 00:19:37.100
Well, I'm inclined to believe him.

00:19:37.100 --> 00:19:42.190
I believe him. I've known Jimmy and his family a long time. They're good people.

00:19:42.190 --> 00:19:45.190
Sure, they're good people. But that doesn't tip the scales.

00:19:45.190 --> 00:19:47.990
Not with some of my political ambitions.

00:19:47.990 --> 00:19:50.600
You mean Andy Fulmer?

00:19:50.600 --> 00:19:55.720
Yeah. He's been waiting for this kind of thing to happen ever since he declared for mayor.

00:19:55.720 --> 00:19:58.580
Come on, George.

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:12.520
Jimmy, Jimmy's gonna be on protection, Jimmy.

00:20:12.890 --> 00:20:14.200
You'd be better off.

00:20:15.480 --> 00:20:15.840
I understand.

00:20:21.300 --> 00:20:24.720
You're expected of murder in the streets.

00:20:25.630 --> 00:20:26.420
I know.

00:20:42.030 --> 00:20:42.830
All right, Dewey, Sandy, man.

00:20:51.130 --> 00:21:00.000
All of our sympathies.

00:21:00.000 --> 00:21:06.630
with you, Mr. Ridley. I want you to know how deeply we feel for the year of your great loss.

00:21:06.630 --> 00:21:15.250
Thank you. It's a tragedy, Mr. Ridley. It's a real tragedy. If we hadn't let the bars down

00:21:15.250 --> 00:21:21.020
in the first place, a thing like this couldn't ever have happened. Now, you know me, Mr. Ridley.

00:21:21.020 --> 00:21:29.380
I speak my mind plain. Your daughter went out with lots of American boys, didn't you? Just a pretty little thing like her.

00:21:30.060 --> 00:21:38.820
and did any of those American boys ever act any way other than they shot her down in cold blood?

00:21:38.820 --> 00:21:42.070
There's something I think you should know.

00:21:42.070 --> 00:21:44.940
That boy didn't kill my daughter.

00:21:44.940 --> 00:21:47.270
It was an accident.

00:21:47.270 --> 00:21:48.930
I had the gun.

00:21:48.930 --> 00:21:50.360
The gun went off.

00:21:50.360 --> 00:21:53.690
The boy didn't kill my daughter, Randy.

00:21:53.690 --> 00:21:55.280
I did.

00:21:55.280 --> 00:21:58.920
Now you just sit there, Mr. Ridley.

00:21:58.920 --> 00:22:00.000
You had a very...

00:22:00.030 --> 00:22:04.870
day. Jesse, haven't you got some work to do?

00:22:07.290 --> 00:22:16.830
Sure, Andy. You know, sometimes when

00:22:16.830 --> 00:22:18.490
a man suffers a great tragedy,

00:22:19.260 --> 00:22:20.560
it can affect his mind.

00:22:21.170 --> 00:22:22.730
You understand that, don't you, Mr. Riddler?

00:22:24.230 --> 00:22:26.980
And in his grief,

00:22:27.140 --> 00:22:29.060
he might forget things,

00:22:30.440 --> 00:22:32.930
Or even imagine things that never really happened.

00:22:34.130 --> 00:22:35.660
Yes, yes, that's true.

00:22:38.590 --> 00:22:40.840
I'm sorry to say this, old friend,

00:22:41.450 --> 00:22:47.360
but I see signs of that in your eagerness to do what's right.

00:22:47.890 --> 00:22:50.650
You're willing to shoulder all the blame for Sally's death.

00:22:51.480 --> 00:22:52.500
Well, shouldn't I?

00:22:52.560 --> 00:22:55.770
No, let's face the truth.

00:22:56.770 --> 00:22:59.570
Didn't that boy, that James, change?

00:23:00.600 --> 00:23:12.860
provoke while he's dead. As the Lord is my judge, that boy caused Sally to die. Yes, and our city's

00:23:12.860 --> 00:23:17.470
overrun with these undesirables, and that breeds the sort of thing that happened to you, and every

00:23:17.470 --> 00:23:21.890
decent citizen in this town wants to see that that don't never happen again. Now, ain't that right,

00:23:21.990 --> 00:23:29.530
Mr. Ridley? Yes, yes, Andy. Now let's you and me sit down and

00:23:30.480 --> 00:23:33.220
Examine what's really right for Virginia City.

00:23:33.220 --> 00:23:39.060
You asked me to order members of our town to fight, if it be, to protect your son.

00:23:39.060 --> 00:23:46.900
My son has not killed anyone. He has committed but one crime. He is Chinese.

00:23:46.900 --> 00:23:52.600
Is James Chang Chinese? Has he not given up the ways of his ancestors?

00:23:52.600 --> 00:23:56.570
Has he not taken the dress and the custom of another people?

00:23:56.570 --> 00:24:00.000
He is ambitious. He desires to educate himself in this country.

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:05.990
this new land. He knows that one day the Chinese will take their place alongside other people

00:24:05.990 --> 00:24:12.370
who have come from many other places to make this great country. Eyes can see great distances

00:24:12.370 --> 00:24:21.650
and risk is the privilege of youth. Your son has accepted the new ways and with this he

00:24:21.650 --> 00:24:29.150
has accepted the risk. He is my son and they talk in the streets of killing him. It is written

00:24:30.000 --> 00:24:35.510
It is better to sacrifice one lamb than to cause the slaughter of the entire flock.

00:24:35.510 --> 00:24:45.240
Some men will fight and save a lamb.

00:24:45.240 --> 00:25:00.000
Thank you, folks. This is an official request, and I expect order continuous to be left.

00:25:02.560 --> 00:25:09.720
I've seen this Chinese boy carrying on with Sally Riddick, so naturally I went and told her father. You know the rest.

00:25:09.720 --> 00:25:13.670
I've been taking enough offer granted here.

00:25:13.670 --> 00:25:18.760
Now, surely, Your Honor. Ben Cartwright's been around long enough to know the facts when he hears them.

00:25:18.760 --> 00:25:26.540
But this is not a trial, Andy. It's an inquest. Is that all?

00:25:26.540 --> 00:25:29.980
Well, ain't that enough, Your Honor?

00:25:30.060 --> 00:25:31.060
Start with me, son.

00:25:31.060 --> 00:25:34.130
Uh, you just get down and let's have the next witness.

00:25:34.130 --> 00:25:49.500
Now, Amanda, just tell us in your own words what happened last night.

00:25:49.500 --> 00:25:52.380
Jimmy Chang killed my sister.

00:26:00.410 --> 00:26:04.540
Amanda, we're not passing judgment here. We're just trying to get the facts.

00:26:05.420 --> 00:26:09.650
Well, what did you expect? Everybody in town knows what kind of a girl my sister was.

00:26:10.280 --> 00:26:13.700
Was flutting herself, fluffing her hands and her own boys.

00:26:15.030 --> 00:26:19.300
What's the matter with her? Jealous of her own sister?

00:26:22.690 --> 00:26:26.720
Please, Amanda. I know how hard this must be for you.

00:26:28.250 --> 00:26:30.000
What a year is what you saw.

00:26:31.660 --> 00:26:42.360
I heard a shot. I ran to the stable. There was Jimmy Chang bending over my sister. There was a gun next to him. Poor father was standing there, just staring.

00:26:43.480 --> 00:26:45.040
And the gun was by Jimmy Chang?

00:26:45.360 --> 00:26:48.010
It was right by him. Right where he dropped it.

00:26:48.010 --> 00:27:00.000
Now we know that was Jimmy Chang's gun. Now, you're not trying to tell us that gun just fell out of the sky. I'm not going to put up.

00:27:00.120 --> 00:27:12.700
Mr. Ridley, will you take the stand?

00:27:20.270 --> 00:27:23.670
Mr. Ridley, do you feel the testimony you've heard here

00:27:23.670 --> 00:27:25.540
is substantial of the way it happened?

00:27:26.810 --> 00:27:29.950
As the Lord is my witness, that book

00:27:30.000 --> 00:27:31.220
caused the death of my daughter.

00:27:32.820 --> 00:27:33.540
Thank you, Mr. Ridley.

00:27:33.830 --> 00:27:34.530
You've messed up, Doc.

00:27:37.430 --> 00:27:38.730
Jimmy Chang, stand up.

00:27:41.650 --> 00:27:42.910
It is the finding of this inquiry

00:27:42.910 --> 00:27:44.250
that you, Jimmy Chang,

00:27:44.880 --> 00:27:46.920
stand trial for the murder of Tyler Ridley.

00:27:48.710 --> 00:27:49.710
Inquest adjourned.

00:27:53.780 --> 00:27:55.700
Sure don't want to miss that trial.

00:27:56.490 --> 00:27:57.970
Well, hang it for sure, won't you, Mr. Fool?

00:27:59.100 --> 00:28:00.000
That's hard to tell.

00:28:00.000 --> 00:28:04.580
Jury trial? Sometimes you just can't depend on a jury.

00:28:04.580 --> 00:28:09.760
Like I told you boys before, when I take over this town, I want it clean.

00:28:09.760 --> 00:28:16.740
Maybe, maybe we ought to see to it, there ain't no trial, boss.

00:28:16.740 --> 00:28:21.050
Jesse, I sure like the way you think.

00:28:30.410 --> 00:28:47.170
...allegation to this town, boy. That's my way of thinking exactly. What are you thinking? I wouldn't be running for mayor.

00:28:47.170 --> 00:28:52.960
One thing, Andy. I ain't a man to jump into things, you know.

00:28:52.960 --> 00:28:58.060
Well, you ain't a man to stand by and watch your own house burn down without tossing on a pail of water either, are you, Cyrus?

00:28:58.060 --> 00:28:59.490
I don't know.

00:29:00.800 --> 00:29:03.630
We let that Chinaman get away with killin' that white girl.

00:29:03.630 --> 00:29:07.960
It's just the same as saying we don't even care what happens to our wives and daughters.

00:29:07.960 --> 00:29:12.040
What do you think we ought to do, Manny?

00:29:12.040 --> 00:29:15.770
I think we ought to put a stop to it right now.

00:29:15.770 --> 00:29:24.960
Looks like you're a little off the game today, Little Joe.

00:29:39.980 --> 00:29:43.670
Fulmer in the height of his glory, so-called.

00:29:43.670 --> 00:29:48.500
Where do you think it'll come to, Pa?

00:29:48.500 --> 00:29:53.860
I don't know, but if Fulmer can fire up that crowd enough, they'll sure enough try to break Jimmy out of jail.

00:29:53.860 --> 00:29:56.100
Oh, don't you think we can hold him off, Pa?

00:29:56.100 --> 00:29:59.700
Nah, I've got no right to ask you current rights to get mixed up in this thing.

00:30:00.250 --> 00:30:01.700
You got no help either, have you?

00:30:01.700 --> 00:30:07.460
You don't have to throw me out. Jimmy Chang's a friend of mine.

00:30:07.460 --> 00:30:10.940
Well, sir?

00:30:10.940 --> 00:30:19.560
I won't lie and say that I'm not pleased, but to make this thing wiggle like, I'd better screw you all in as deputy.

00:30:19.560 --> 00:30:25.370
That's good. He's dead one. Deputy Badger's in here.

00:30:43.820 --> 00:30:44.640
It's like you were right.

00:30:46.300 --> 00:30:48.600
I don't think there's any more doubt about it, Chuck.

00:30:53.490 --> 00:30:58.580
Fast.

00:31:00.640 --> 00:31:03.480
Well, you can't rightly let them come in and lynch your mother, can you?

00:31:03.480 --> 00:31:07.230
Then, Jimmy Chang has been indicted for murder.

00:31:07.230 --> 00:31:12.200
It's my sworn duty to uphold the law, and it's also the sworn duty of you and your sons now.

00:31:12.200 --> 00:31:14.090
What are we supposed to do, sit here and wait?

00:31:14.090 --> 00:31:15.670
That's the way it is.

00:31:15.670 --> 00:31:19.660
Even if we get Jimmy out, we gotta get him past those men.

00:31:19.660 --> 00:31:27.770
Yeah, I suppose nothing would make Fuller happier than to kill Jimmy Chang while attempting to break jail.

00:31:27.770 --> 00:31:30.000
I look great, there's no law that says...

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:35.100
a deputy can't walk out of here, sir. No, there isn't. If you boys want to change your mind,

00:31:35.160 --> 00:31:39.290
I can release you from any obligations. No, that's not what I meant. I just don't like

00:31:39.290 --> 00:31:43.680
the idea of sitting around here while Andy Palmer calls every turn. What's in your mind,

00:31:43.760 --> 00:31:47.850
son? Papa, I can't help thinking about Amanda and the way she behaved on a witness stand.

00:31:48.520 --> 00:31:51.980
Now, I've known her a long time. I just don't believe she's turned that bitter.

00:31:52.460 --> 00:31:55.340
You think you might want to talk to her? I'd like to try.

00:31:56.500 --> 00:32:00.000
It's worth a chance. Maybe through her

00:32:00.000 --> 00:32:01.260
you could break down Ridley's story.

00:32:06.180 --> 00:32:07.930
I don't like you going out there, though.

00:32:08.720 --> 00:32:10.040
A horse and I could cover him, Pop.

00:32:10.250 --> 00:32:11.870
Oh, that'd be playing right in the Fulmer's hands.

00:32:12.230 --> 00:32:14.450
And there'd be three less guns in here

00:32:14.450 --> 00:32:15.230
for him to worry about.

00:32:15.600 --> 00:32:16.600
I'll get through all right, Pop.

00:32:17.020 --> 00:32:19.080
I wasn't thinking of you getting through, Adam.

00:32:19.140 --> 00:32:20.380
I was thinking of you getting back in.

00:32:21.770 --> 00:32:22.890
Don't sell Fulmer short.

00:32:23.340 --> 00:32:24.580
He's got Ridley on his side,

00:32:24.620 --> 00:32:25.640
and he's gonna do everything in his power

00:32:25.640 --> 00:32:26.280
to keep him there.

00:32:27.030 --> 00:32:27.910
Well, I'm gonna risk it.

00:32:53.320 --> 00:32:54.280
That's an Atticott, right?

00:32:54.600 --> 00:32:57.230
The stink of that woman killer get too thick for-

00:32:57.230 --> 00:32:58.930
You get out of my way.

00:33:02.330 --> 00:33:03.490
You're a proddy, Adam.

00:33:03.860 --> 00:33:05.780
Ain't no law says we can't stand out here in the street.

00:33:06.630 --> 00:33:07.910
Yeah, why are your card rights so nervous?

00:33:08.250 --> 00:33:08.900
You ain't doing nothing.

00:33:10.530 --> 00:33:11.610
Well, just keep on doing it.

00:33:19.850 --> 00:33:28.260
Can I come in?

00:33:30.030 --> 00:33:30.900
I suppose it'd be all right.

00:33:41.010 --> 00:33:42.690
Well, it's really you I want to talk to, Amanda.

00:33:43.000 --> 00:33:44.530
She likes to die.

00:33:45.550 --> 00:33:50.910
Well, if your steps might have good times in this house.

00:33:51.730 --> 00:33:53.370
We haven't entertained since Mother died.

00:33:56.470 --> 00:33:57.820
Seven years?

00:33:58.400 --> 00:34:00.000
Must get kind of lonely for you sometimes.

00:34:01.920 --> 00:34:05.350
I had obligations. I assume those obligations.

00:34:07.310 --> 00:34:08.670
Have to be at such a high price?

00:34:10.650 --> 00:34:13.250
You think it's been easy keeping the household together with Mother gone?

00:34:15.070 --> 00:34:19.140
No, I don't. I watched my own father do it for years.

00:34:20.320 --> 00:34:23.040
Yes, but Sally did everything she could to make things difficult.

00:34:24.520 --> 00:34:26.260
Yeah, Pa had his moments with all of us, too.

00:34:26.830 --> 00:34:29.750
She had no respect for anything, not for me or for my father.

00:34:30.480 --> 00:34:35.280
Amanda, stop feeling sorry for yourself. Life hasn't passed you by.

00:34:35.280 --> 00:34:38.280
Why can't you Cartwright's mind your business and let us mind ours?

00:34:38.280 --> 00:34:41.280
Because it happens to be everybody's business when a boy's life's at stake.

00:34:41.280 --> 00:34:49.630
You can stand there because my sister's been murdered. What do you expect me to do when I'm over there to Jimmy Chang and tell him it was all a big mistake?

00:34:49.630 --> 00:34:53.900
If that's what it was, yes. Jimmy Chang said he didn't have a gun. He said it was an accident.

00:34:53.900 --> 00:34:59.330
Now look Amanda, I've always admired you because you had the courage to stand up for what you thought was right.

00:35:00.190 --> 00:35:03.310
Sally was just exactly the way you used to be. No more, no less.

00:35:05.140 --> 00:35:06.620
You don't need to pretend with me, Amanda.

00:35:14.060 --> 00:35:23.780
Then, so long. What should I do?

00:35:24.930 --> 00:35:25.890
Tell the truth.

00:35:27.000 --> 00:35:28.700
What are you doing in my house, Cockright?

00:35:29.690 --> 00:35:30.000
There's no...

00:35:30.090 --> 00:35:33.820
Fulmer's safe in this town? How dare you persecute my daughter?

00:35:34.550 --> 00:35:40.050
It's not your daughter that's being persecuted. There's a young boy over in that jail that's just about to face a lynch mob.

00:35:40.480 --> 00:35:44.440
My boy's a murderer and a heathen. He's been indicted for his crime.

00:35:44.640 --> 00:35:48.830
Indicted, but not convicted. Why don't you think Jimmy Chang deserves a fair trial?

00:35:50.490 --> 00:35:52.320
James Chang will have a fair trial?

00:35:52.620 --> 00:35:55.040
Not unless you tell Andy Fulmer that's what you want him to have.

00:35:56.100 --> 00:35:59.440
Oh, Mr. Fulmer's an honorable man. He doesn't need me to tell him what to do.

00:36:00.410 --> 00:36:02.000
What's the matter, Mr. Ridley?

00:36:02.000 --> 00:36:11.480
You're afraid to face up to Andy Fulmer the principles you value so highly?

00:36:11.480 --> 00:36:14.020
Fear no man.

00:36:14.020 --> 00:36:18.170
Well, then talk to him.

00:36:18.170 --> 00:36:30.000
I'll go with you, Father.

00:36:30.960 --> 00:36:32.210
He ain't even no citizen.

00:36:32.210 --> 00:36:36.600
Those Cartwrights tell us how to run our town, they don't live in Virginia City.

00:36:36.600 --> 00:36:39.160
And this town is for us that lives here, for us Americans.

00:36:39.160 --> 00:36:42.650
There are only three Cartwrights in there.

00:36:42.650 --> 00:36:47.050
Adam left, and we'll see to it if he don't get back in again.

00:36:47.050 --> 00:36:48.650
I say march to the jail.

00:36:48.650 --> 00:36:56.450
Sheriff Paulson.

00:36:56.450 --> 00:36:57.810
Well, are you up to Cartwrights?

00:36:57.810 --> 00:37:00.000
He's down for a walk with some friends.

00:37:00.000 --> 00:37:03.010
Fine, just so you seem nervous.

00:37:03.010 --> 00:37:08.510
Mr. Ridley, is Adam trying to force you to do something against your will?

00:37:08.510 --> 00:37:13.410
No man forces me against my will.

00:37:13.410 --> 00:37:15.320
Talk with Mr. Fulmer.

00:37:15.320 --> 00:37:22.690
Talk to me and get those people out there.

00:37:22.690 --> 00:37:24.610
I certainly dare. You're not a man in this town.

00:37:24.610 --> 00:37:26.610
Can't speak to me whenever he wants you. Come right on in.

00:37:26.610 --> 00:37:27.660
Ms. Mander?

00:37:37.680 --> 00:37:40.920
Let's step into my private office. We can talk freely there.

00:37:41.450 --> 00:37:42.250
I'll wait out here.

00:38:02.910 --> 00:38:07.960
Now then, what was it you wanted to say to me, J.R.?

00:38:07.960 --> 00:38:10.100
I want those people out there to know the truth.

00:38:10.660 --> 00:38:12.660
I want to tell them what I told you this morning.

00:38:13.360 --> 00:38:15.910
And what did you tell me this morning, J.R.?

00:38:15.910 --> 00:38:17.600
Why, that Jimmy Chang is innocent.

00:38:18.230 --> 00:38:19.870
That my daughter's death was an accident.

00:38:20.570 --> 00:38:22.270
And what did I say then, Mr. Ridley?

00:38:23.740 --> 00:38:24.820
I just don't remember.

00:38:25.420 --> 00:38:27.160
Didn't I say that I wanted to help you?

00:38:27.600 --> 00:38:30.000
Didn't I say that the people of Virginia City were behind me?

00:38:30.190 --> 00:38:33.790
100%. Did you see all those people out there in that street?

00:38:34.630 --> 00:38:38.740
Why do you think they're there? They're there because they're your friends, J.R.

00:38:39.070 --> 00:38:42.820
Just as I'm your friend. Because we both believe in the same

00:38:42.820 --> 00:38:46.380
principles. We believe in honesty and decency

00:38:46.380 --> 00:38:51.020
and the American way. Now, ain't that right, Mr. Ridley? Yes.

00:38:51.370 --> 00:38:56.210
I suppose so. Now, you don't suppose. You know. Those people

00:38:56.210 --> 00:39:00.000
are out there because they're your friends. They're out there to

00:39:00.000 --> 00:39:27.460
honor you. They're there to honor the man who stood up in his hour of great tragedy, not for his own sake, but for the sake of an entire city. Now are you going to let them down, J.R.? Are you going to let your daughter die in vain? They're waiting for you out there, J.R.

00:39:36.240 --> 00:39:42.800
Well, Mr Ridley, I have no right to stand in the way of my friends, the people here in Virginia City.

00:39:43.310 --> 00:39:47.930
Like I say, J.R., I like your ideas fine. You talk to me any time. The door's always open.

00:39:52.650 --> 00:39:53.350
What happened in there?

00:39:54.330 --> 00:39:58.220
It was horrible. It's as if my father has no mind of his own.

00:39:59.090 --> 00:40:00.000
Well, I'll change his mind.

00:40:03.550 --> 00:40:05.690
Make him understand that he's got to tell the truth.

00:40:06.560 --> 00:40:07.620
All right, if you think you can.

00:40:08.850 --> 00:40:12.550
Remember, Amanda, Jimmy Chang's life depends on your father telling the truth.

00:40:13.930 --> 00:40:15.210
I realize that now, Adam.

00:40:15.780 --> 00:40:16.520
Come on, Amanda.

00:40:34.640 --> 00:40:35.860
Why don't you leave those folks alone?

00:40:47.820 --> 00:40:52.780
Cartwright here seemed to be, and we figured he was planning to pester the Hoodleys some more.

00:40:53.750 --> 00:40:55.150
Boys, put those guns away.

00:40:55.780 --> 00:40:57.540
Jesse, you know we're not men of violence.

00:40:58.520 --> 00:41:00.000
You go right ahead, Mr. Cartwright.

00:41:00.410 --> 00:41:01.430
Just do whatever you like.

00:41:02.890 --> 00:41:04.390
I'll do just exactly that, Mr. Paul.

00:41:07.720 --> 00:41:10.230
You sure you don't want me to stop him, boss?

00:41:10.770 --> 00:41:12.140
Why should you do that, Jesse?

00:41:12.450 --> 00:41:20.280
Just when we got things right, we're...

00:41:20.280 --> 00:41:22.400
Will you taste anything like you still have beans?

00:41:24.010 --> 00:41:24.250
Yeah.

00:41:25.180 --> 00:41:26.240
No, I'm trying not to remember.

00:41:26.870 --> 00:41:29.430
What you mean to say is you...

00:41:30.250 --> 00:41:32.180
Remember, tasting anything is good, don't you?

00:41:32.180 --> 00:41:39.690
Yeah, that's right with this kind of chow.

00:41:39.690 --> 00:41:43.240
Goodbye to yours, why don't you try to get some of that down?

00:41:43.240 --> 00:41:45.630
Thanks, Cos, but I'm not hungry.

00:41:45.630 --> 00:41:48.030
Hungry? What's that got to do with it?

00:41:48.030 --> 00:41:49.980
Think the only time a man can eat when he's hungry?

00:41:49.980 --> 00:41:53.960
Yeah, you haven't got any kind of fool idea like that, don't you?

00:41:53.960 --> 00:41:56.540
I killed Sally.

00:41:56.540 --> 00:41:58.580
You believe me, George?

00:42:01.720 --> 00:42:04.500
Jimmy, y'all have more sense to even ask such questions.

00:42:04.500 --> 00:42:09.510
There are some people in this town. How can they, Hoss?

00:42:09.510 --> 00:42:14.420
Jimmy, don't you worry about it. You've got lots of friends in this town.

00:42:14.420 --> 00:42:16.700
Friends aren't a lot you think.

00:42:16.700 --> 00:42:28.990
Here it comes. I really thought they tried to stop you from getting you back in.

00:42:28.990 --> 00:42:29.910
I'm so sure.

00:42:30.030 --> 00:42:31.340
he figured he didn't have to.

00:42:31.340 --> 00:42:33.610
What about Amanda? Did you find out anything from her?

00:42:33.610 --> 00:42:35.560
Oh, I sure did.

00:42:35.560 --> 00:42:37.880
I mean, I've convinced her she should tell the truth.

00:42:37.880 --> 00:42:42.270
I thought we had Ridley convinced and then we got over to Forrest and...

00:42:42.270 --> 00:42:45.520
I don't know, Forrest's got some strange kind of hole on the man.

00:42:45.520 --> 00:42:47.820
He's like so much clay in his hands.

00:42:47.820 --> 00:42:50.150
I think Amanda's still working on him.

00:42:50.150 --> 00:42:52.490
What, do you think she'll get anywhere with him?

00:42:52.490 --> 00:42:54.870
Well, if she doesn't, we've got a lynch mob on her hands.

00:43:00.000 --> 00:43:02.240
and make you understand me to you.

00:43:02.240 --> 00:43:04.760
I'm on the side of right.

00:43:04.760 --> 00:43:08.120
Right? You're just doing what Andy Fuller wants you to do.

00:43:08.120 --> 00:43:10.250
That boy's gonna die!

00:43:10.250 --> 00:43:12.680
Your sister died too, didn't she?

00:43:12.680 --> 00:43:14.660
Yes, she did.

00:43:14.660 --> 00:43:20.200
Until now, I don't believe I really care.

00:43:20.200 --> 00:43:24.710
You speak like that to me?

00:43:24.710 --> 00:43:27.270
I speak like that because it's the truth.

00:43:27.270 --> 00:43:29.390
Your sister brought a disgrace on us!

00:43:32.300 --> 00:43:44.740
Is it really Jimmy Chang, your father?

00:43:47.320 --> 00:43:48.900
Was her death really an accident?

00:43:49.680 --> 00:43:51.750
Or did you pull that trigger on purpose?

00:43:55.030 --> 00:43:56.500
Is that why you're afraid to talk?

00:44:00.670 --> 00:44:03.550
As God is my witness, it was an accident.

00:44:04.500 --> 00:44:10.420
Then God lied to us.

00:44:11.950 --> 00:44:14.610
We never really believed the things we said about Sally.

00:44:15.160 --> 00:44:23.660
And if we let Jimmy Chang do it, we would really be condemning Sally, Father, where the guilty was.

00:44:37.930 --> 00:44:39.890
I'm just interested in doing what's right.

00:44:40.020 --> 00:44:43.570
Let's step between us and what we know is right.

00:44:44.180 --> 00:44:45.300
Let's say let's rush him and get him.

00:44:50.840 --> 00:45:00.000
Let's put a few shots away.

00:45:00.000 --> 00:45:29.550
Really? It looks like she can't instantly.

00:45:32.590 --> 00:45:34.070
J.R., those cartwrights will kill ya.

00:45:34.070 --> 00:45:36.570
It isn't the cartwrights this town needs to fear, Fulmer.

00:45:36.790 --> 00:45:39.090
Ah, J.R., we understand each other.

00:45:39.090 --> 00:45:40.330
That won't work again, Andy.

00:45:41.010 --> 00:45:42.810
I'm gonna tell Sheriff Halstead the truth.

00:45:42.980 --> 00:45:44.400
Now, we've been through this before.

00:45:44.640 --> 00:45:46.380
I'm going to tell him the truth.

00:45:49.540 --> 00:45:51.220
Get him.

00:46:00.000 --> 00:46:04.200
- Why did you kill him? - What are you saying? You told me to kill him.

00:46:04.200 --> 00:46:15.750
Murder. Filthy, Jesse!

00:46:36.780 --> 00:46:38.720
My father wanted to tell you something.

00:46:38.720 --> 00:46:51.730
If you didn't have any gun, he killed Sally.

00:46:51.730 --> 00:46:53.560
That's what he wanted to tell you.

00:46:53.560 --> 00:46:58.870
Well, Palma...

00:47:00.000 --> 00:47:10.500
Three dead. You satisfied? Trying to murder this town? You still want this man before me?

00:47:10.500 --> 00:47:21.190
This is a terrible thing that's happened here today. We sure don't want anything like that.

00:47:43.920 --> 00:47:47.440
I need your liberty, Mr. Chet.

00:47:47.440 --> 00:47:56.970
Come, you don't got to worry about it.

00:47:56.970 --> 00:47:57.520
Yes, sir.

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:00.540
That is Jay.
